---
/**
 * WikiTip — About & Methodology. (wiki-tip.com/about)
 *
 * ── 왜 만드나 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `/about` 이 **404 였다.** 구글은 발행 주체를 확인할 수 없는 사이트를 올려 주지 않는다.
 * 우리의 유일한 마케팅이 검색 유입인데, 그 문이 닫혀 있었다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 언론사가 아니다 ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * 사장님 지시(2026-08-04): 「**아직은 언론사 아님에 유의**」
 * 인터넷신문 등록 전이다. 그래서 이 지면에서
 *   ① 「news outlet」 「newsroom」 「journalist」 를 쓰지 않는다
 *   ② 언론사 자격에 딸린 관행(소속사 배포 사진 이용 등)에 기대지 않는다
 *   ③ 대신 **우리가 무엇인지를 정확히 적는다** — 공개 데이터를 세는 곳이다
 * 등록하면 이 파일과 `WikiTip.astro` 꼬리말을 함께 고친다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 광고 없음 ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Riot Production 심사 중(App 866800). 승인 전 광고는 API 영구 취소 사유다.
 * 「광고로 운영한다」고도 적지 않는다 — 지금 사실이 아니다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../../consts';

const TITLE = 'About & methodology';
const DESC =
  'Who publishes WikiTip, exactly which public datasets each number comes from, '
  + 'how we decide what counts as a Korean production, and what we deliberately leave out.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  url: 'https://wiki-tip.com/about',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'WikiTip',
    url: 'https://wiki-tip.com/',
    parentOrganization: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      legalName: PUBLISHER.legalName,
      address: PUBLISHER.address,
      email: PUBLISHER.email,
      foundingDate: String(PUBLISHER.foundedYear),
    },
  },
};
---

{/*
  ⚠ `canonical` 을 일부러 걸지 않았다. **wiki-tip.com 은 아직 우리 것이 아니다** —
    2026-08-04 12:59 KST 실측으로 `302 → errdoc.gabia.io/403.html` 이다.
    NS 가 tosana/ines(가비아가 만든 Cloudflare 존)로 가 있어 우리 존(kami/keenan)이
    권한을 못 갖는다. 죽은 주소를 canonical 로 걸면 색인에서 통째로 빠진다.
  ⚠ `noindex` 도 같은 이유다. 지면이 부실해서가 아니라 **주소가 아직 안 살아서**다.
    → NS 가 kami/keenan 으로 바뀌고 `curl https://wiki-tip.com/about` 이 200 이 되면
      이 파일에서 `noindex` 를 빼고 canonical 을 되살린다. 둘을 같이 푼다.
*/}
<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} noindex>
  <h1>About &amp; methodology</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    WikiTip counts what public datasets already publish about Korean pop culture, names every
    source, and states what it left out. It does not report rumours, reprint press releases,
    or rank anything it cannot show the arithmetic for.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      Korean drama, film, music and esports are followed closely across Southeast Asia and the
      wider English-speaking world, but almost everything written about them in English is
      either translated gossip or a repackaged press release. Meanwhile the numbers that would
      settle most arguments — how many countries a title actually charted in, how many hours it
      was actually watched, how many people actually look a performer up — are published openly
      and read by almost nobody.
    </p>
    <p>
      That gap is the whole idea. We take feeds that are already public, count them the same way
      every week, and publish the count with its source attached.
    </p>
    <p class="callout">
      <b>WikiTip is not a registered news outlet.</b> It is a data publication operated by the
      company named at the foot of this page. We do not employ reporters, we do not conduct
      interviews, and we do not claim press credentials or the access that comes with them.
      Everything here is derived from datasets anyone can download.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where each number comes from</h2>
    <p>Every figure on this site traces to one of four sources. There are no others.</p>
    <ul class="src">
      <li>
        <b>Netflix Top 10 (Tudum)</b> — the official weekly TSV releases covering 94 countries
        and every week since July 2021. Netflix publishes hours viewed and country rank itself;
        we do not estimate either.
        <a href="https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10" rel="external noopener" target="_blank">netflix.com/tudum/top10</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Wikidata</b> — country of origin (property P495), cast member (P161) and country of
        citizenship (P27). This is what tells us a title is a Korean production and a performer
        is Korean, rather than us deciding it.
        <a href="https://query.wikidata.org/" rel="external noopener" target="_blank">query.wikidata.org</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Wikimedia Pageviews API</b> — daily English Wikipedia article views, human traffic
        only, automated and spider traffic excluded by the API itself.
        <a href="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/" rel="external noopener" target="_blank">wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Riot Games API</b> — ranked ladder counts across six regions, collected once a day
        under a registered application. A ladder cannot be reconstructed after the fact, so a
        day we fail to collect is simply missing and we say so rather than interpolating.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      All four are used within their published terms. We do not scrape sites that disallow it,
      we do not resell any feed, and we do not republish a source's data table wholesale — what
      we publish is a count derived from it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we decide something is Korean</h2>
    <p>
      This decides what appears on the site, so it should not be a judgement call. It is not one.
      A title counts as a Korean production when Wikidata's country-of-origin field lists South
      Korea; a performer counts as Korean when the country-of-citizenship field says so.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two consequences worth knowing. International co-productions that list Korea alongside
      other countries <em>are</em> included — <i>Snowpiercer</i> and <i>Mickey 17</i> both
      qualify. And because cast lists on those titles include performers of every nationality,
      the citizenship filter is applied separately at the performer level; without it, an actor
      ranking built from Korean films fills up with people who are not Korean. We found exactly
      that in our first roster and corrected it, which cut the list from 1,553 names to 1,344.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Where a title has no Wikidata entry, it is absent rather than guessed at. That biases the
      list slightly toward well-documented titles, and we would rather have that bias visible
      than fix it by hand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the numbers do not mean</h2>
    <ul class="src">
      <li>
        <b>Attention is not popularity.</b> A Wikipedia page climbs for good news and bad — an
        award, a casting, a scandal, a death. We publish the count and the window it covers. We
        do not publish a reason, because the count does not contain one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Hours viewed is not quality, and not audience size either.</b> A long series
        accumulates hours a film cannot. We report the figure Netflix publishes and label it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Netflix is not streaming.</b> No other service publishes a comparable weekly ranking,
        so a title absent here may simply be somewhere else. Broadcast ratings are a separate
        measurement system and are not mixed in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>A missing performer is not an unpopular one.</b> Anyone without an English Wikipedia
        article cannot be measured by pageviews at all. The front page states how many of our
        roster that affects.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Photographs</h2>
    <p>
      We do not publish agency, label or studio photographs. Korean outlets routinely use
      officially distributed press images, but that practice rests on being a registered press
      organisation, and we are not one yet. Rather than borrow a permission we do not hold, the
      graphics on this site are built from our own counts — charts we made, of numbers we
      calculated, which nobody else owns.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a number here is wrong we want to know, and a correction is cheap because every figure
      has a named source you can check against us. Write to
      <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.email}`}>{PUBLISHER.email}</a>. Substantive corrections are
      made in place with a visible date. We do not quietly rewrite published figures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      WikiTip is free to read and carries no advertising. We accept no sponsored placements, no
      paid coverage, and no payment from any agency, label, studio or platform. We are not
      affiliated with, endorsed by, or licensed by any of them.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      WikiTip is not endorsed by Riot Games and does not reflect the views or opinions of Riot
      Games or anyone officially involved in producing or managing Riot Games properties.
      Riot Games and all associated properties are trademarks or registered trademarks of
      Riot Games, Inc.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <p class="pub">
      <b>{PUBLISHER.legalName}</b><br />
      Representative director: {PUBLISHER.representative}<br />
      {PUBLISHER.address}<br />
      Business registration number {PUBLISHER.bizRegNo}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.email}`}>{PUBLISHER.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      The same company publishes <a href="https://seoulmarkets.com/">SeoulMarkets</a>, which
      covers Korean financial markets in English, and <a href="https://100yearmap.com/">백년지도</a>,
      a Korean-language guide to what happens after university.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.6rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  p { margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .pub { line-height: 1.9; }

  /* 「언론사가 아니다」는 묻히면 안 된다. 본문 흐름에서 한 칸 띄워 세운다 */
  .callout {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--card);
    padding: .9rem 1rem; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .src { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .src li {
    padding: .7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .src li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .src a { color: var(--accent); }

  .back { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
